            "compiled_code": "-- One row per player per charted match.\n--\n-- The seed carries a row per set ('1'..'5') plus a 'Total' row that already\n-- sums them, so anything but set = 'Total' double-counts.\n--\n-- 13 matches were charted twice. A handful are byte-identical, but the rest\n-- disagree slightly (two volunteers counting the same match), so distinct\n-- won't collapse them -- qualify picks one charting deterministically.\n-- ponytail: highest serve_pts wins the tie; swap the order by if you'd\n-- rather reconcile the two chartings properly.\nwith source as (\n    select * from `gary-yiu-001`.`tennis_match`.`raw_match_stats`\n    where `set` = 'Total'\n)\n\nselect\n    match_id,\n    player,\n    serve_pts,\n    aces,\n    dfs,\n    first_in,\n    first_won,\n    second_in,\n    second_won,\n    bk_pts,\n    bp_saved,\n    return_pts,\n    return_pts_won,\n    winners,\n    unforced\n\nfrom source\nqualify row_number() over (\n    partition by match_id, player\n    order by serve_pts desc, winners desc\n) = 1",
